-- title:
--   Igusa scheme as two-chart integral model over ℤ_{(ℓ)}
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $\ell$ a prime. Write $R = \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` for the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the nonzero divisors $d \mid N$; let $j =$ `jFull N` be the element of $F$ given by $j(q)$ itself. The Igusa scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) is by definition the pushout of the span `fFin N ℓ` and `fInf N ℓ`, the two morphisms of affine schemes obtained by applying $\operatorname{Spec}$ to the inclusions of the subalgebras `chartAlg` attached to $\{j\}$ and to $\{j^{-1}\}$ into the middle algebra, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the same pushout formed for a general base ring in place of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$. The assertion is that there exists an isomorphism of schemes $e$ from [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) to [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) such that $e$ followed by the structure morphism `TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ equals `igusaTo N ℓ`, and such that each of the two chart morphisms `ιFin N ℓ`, `ιInf N ℓ` into the Igusa scheme, followed by $e$, equals the corresponding chart morphism `TwoChartIntegralModel.ιFin`, `TwoChartIntegralModel.ιInf`.
--
--   This identifies the level-$N$ Igusa scheme over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ with the general two-chart integral model construction applied to the full modular function field and its $j$-invariant, compatibly with the map to the base and with the two chart immersions. It is the bridge allowing results proved for the general two-chart model to be transported to the Igusa scheme, and is used in the pullback and Atkin–Lehner involution statements for [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_nonempty_iso_twoChartIntegralModel.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
